• at any point in time, a company may only appoint one agent to effect any repurchases on the company’s behalf;

• a resolution has been passed by the board confirming that the board has authorised the general repurchase, that the company passed the solvency and liquidity test and that since the test was done there have been no material changes to the financial position of the group, or in the case of a purchase by a subsidiary, a resolution of the board of such subsidiary confirming that such board has authorised the general repurchase, that such subsidiary passed the solvency and liquidity test and that since the test was done there have been no material changes to the financial position of the group;

2.4 Size, spread and stage

Sabcap:

a) aims to invest in good businesses with first-class management without being restricted by any required absolute size or level of percentage holdings;

b) may hold equity instruments that are small in percentage terms but where the Group is able to exercise influence through Board representation or shareholder agreements;

c) may hold majority or joint controlling interests but without direct management responsibility;

d) will not be constrained by any required balance between listed and unlisted holdings;

e) will not be constrained by any required sector spread;

f) will be unlikely to make new investments that exceed 15% of its portfolio or 25% of shareholders’ equity.
